# The published-self-scan fixtures are CAPTURES, byte for byte. They are the
# evidence that a guard can go red, and their exact bytes are part of that
# evidence: a capture that has been line-ending-normalised is a capture of
# something slightly different from what was observed. `-text` stops git from
# converting them in either direction, on any platform.
#
# The rest of the tree is unaffected -- this rule is deliberately narrow, and
# deliberately does NOT say `* -text`, which would turn every source file in
# the repository into a binary as far as git is concerned.
_verify/fixtures/*.out -text
